---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How to Add a WhatsApp Link to Your LinkedIn Profile | LinkWA"
  description="Step-by-step guide to adding a WhatsApp click-to-chat link to your LinkedIn profile. Capture professional networking leads and client inquiries."
  canonical="https://linkwa.in/blog/whatsapp-link-linkedin-profile"
>
<article class="article-wrap">
  <div class="article-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="article-tag">Guide</div>
      <h1>How to Add a WhatsApp Link to Your LinkedIn Profile</h1>
      <div class="article-meta"><span>Jun 18, 2026</span><span>·</span><span>4 min read</span></div>
      <p class="article-intro">Turn your professional networking profile into a direct client acquisition channel. Here is the step-by-step guide to adding a WhatsApp link to your LinkedIn contact info or featured section.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <div class="callout"><strong>Make it simple:</strong> LinkedIn visitors are busy. By offering a direct WhatsApp link, you let potential clients, partners, or recruiters skip the slow InMail process and chat with you immediately.</div>

      <h2>Why add a WhatsApp link to LinkedIn?</h2>
      <p>LinkedIn InMail response rates can be low, and not everyone checks their LinkedIn inbox regularly. On the other hand, WhatsApp messages are read almost instantly. For freelancers, consultants, agency owners, and recruiters, adding a WhatsApp link to LinkedIn removes communication friction and increases lead conversion rates.</p>

      <h2>Where to add the WhatsApp link on LinkedIn</h2>
      <p>You can add your WhatsApp link in three strategic locations on your LinkedIn profile:</p>

      <h3>1. The Contact Info Section</h3>
      <p>This is the most standard location. To add it here:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Click the edit icon on your LinkedIn profile header.</li>
        <li>Scroll down to the <strong>Contact Info</strong> section and click <strong>Edit contact info</strong>.</li>
        <li>Under <strong>Website URL</strong>, paste your LinkWA link.</li>
        <li>Select "Other" or "Portfolio" as the website type, and type "WhatsApp Chat" or "Direct Chat" as the label.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Save</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. The Profile Link (LinkedIn Premium)</h3>
      <p>If you have LinkedIn Premium, you can place a custom button directly below your profile photo and display name. Edit your profile, locate the "Custom button" option under settings, select "Link", paste your WhatsApp link, and enter a call to action like "Message me on WhatsApp".</p>

      <h3>3. The Featured Section</h3>
      <p>Make your link highly visible by adding it as a card in your Featured section. Go to your profile, click "Add profile section", select "Recommended", and click "Add featured". Choose "Link" (+), paste your WhatsApp link, and add a title like "Book a free consultation call". Use a high-quality preview image to make it stand out.</p>

      <h2>Writing the perfect pre-filled message</h2>
      <p>When someone clicks your LinkedIn WhatsApp link, a pre-filled message helps them start the conversation easily. Try template options like:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><i>"Hi [Name], I saw your LinkedIn profile and want to discuss a project."</i></li>
        <li><i>"Hi [Name], I'm interested in booking a consulting session."</i></li>
        <li><i>"Hi! I'd love to connect and discuss professional opportunities."</i></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="article-cta">
      <h3>Create your LinkedIn WhatsApp link</h3>
      <p>Use LinkWA to generate a professional click-to-chat link with a custom message.</p>
      <a href="/" class="article-cta-btn">Open LinkWA →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="article-nav"><a href="/blog" class="back-link">← All articles</a></div>
  </div>
</article>
</Base>
